# Auto-resolve merge conflicts for generated files
# The pre-commit hook regenerates ATTESTATION.md anyway, so conflicts don't matter
ATTESTATION.md merge=ours

# CHANGES.md is append-at-top: every ticket branch inserts its entry directly
# under the header, so N concurrent branches conflict with each other, and each
# merge re-conflicts every branch still open.
#
# The default 3-way merge is worse than useless here. Because every entry uses
# the same "**How to run it.**" and "**Roll back.**" headings, git matches those
# common lines and COLLAPSES two entries into one — so deleting the conflict
# markers welds one ticket's rollback instructions onto another ticket's entry.
# In a file whose whole purpose is telling someone how to undo a change under
# pressure, that is a silent and dangerous defect. It happened on three separate
# branches before this rule existed, and was caught by hand each time.
#
# union keeps every line from both sides, so both entries survive intact. It
# drops the shared `---` separator between them; run
# `node scripts/factory/normalize-changes.mjs` after a union merge to restore it.
# union is not a substitute for reading the resulting diff.
CHANGES.md merge=union
